      <activity id="aecd43d0-a971-51ee-ad79-63985b8a73ed" activityNameId="4d04195d-06a4-5259-8dc1-1d82a7b88d74" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at cogen 300kWth, biomethane, allocation exergy</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at cogen 300kWth, biomethane, allocation exergy
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from biomethane, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 300 kWth. The multioutput process "biomethane, burned in cogen 300kWth delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 300kWth, biomethane, allocation exergy" and "electricity, at cogen 300kWth, biomethane, allocation exergy". The energy efficiency is 38% for electricity and 49% for heat. The exergy factor is 1 for ectricity and 0.170 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.82 for electricity an 0.18 for heat.;
Synonyms: Strom, ab BHKW 300kWth, Biogas, aufbereitet, Allokation Exergie; 
UUID: e153215e-5b20-3008-8366-76412dad6b2a
Included are the biomethane burning in a 300 kWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and allocation according to exergy is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland.
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e153215e-5b20-3008-8366-76412dad6b2a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
